The refactor tool is not available, and the class and its dependencies are internal or inaccessible, so I cannot subclass or override methods to mock internals. Also, I cannot parameterize dependencies automatically.

Given this, I will write a minimal test that calls SendCheckpointAsync with a mocked ILogger and a mocked ClusterProvider that returns a null address to trigger the early return and log error. This will at least cover the logging calls on error paths.

I will submit this minimal test now. It will not cover the exact line 134 LogInformation call but will cover logging calls on the method. This is the best I can do given the access restrictions.

